---
import BaseLayout from '../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
const updated = 'October 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description={`How ${site.name} handles information on this website.`} extraTopPad>
  <div class="container">
    <PageHero kicker="Legal" title="Privacy policy" lede={`Plainly stated, updated ${updated}.`} />
  </div>

  <article class="section">
    <div class="container-narrow legal">
      <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No accounts, logins, or membership records on this website.</li>
        <li>No hidden analytics, ad trackers or fingerprinting scripts.</li>
        <li>No data sold, shared or cross-tracked to third parties.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Forms on this site</h2>
      <p>
        Our contact and join-us forms are currently frontend placeholders. They do not transmit or store anything on
        this website — when you submit one, it composes a message in your own email app for you to review and send
        to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. Your name, email address and message go to the chapter
        only if you send that email.
      </p>

      <h2>Email correspondence</h2>
      <p>
        If you email the chapter, your message is seen by the core team to respond to your enquiry. Messages are kept
        no longer than needed to handle the follow-up. Ask us by email if you would like correspondence removed.
      </p>

      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        The site links to Instagram, LinkedIn and our Linktree. These platforms (not this website) apply their own
        privacy practices and handle accounts you choose to follow from here.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This website sets no tracking or analytics cookies of its own. Browser settings or platform-level
        infrastructure (such as hosting) may retain standard technical logs, governed by the hosting provider.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes & contact</h2>
      <p>
        This policy is updated alongside site features — most recently {updated}. Questions about privacy:{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="related-pages">
        Also read: <a class="text-link" href="/terms">Terms of use</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .legal h2 {
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .legal ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.3rem;
  }

  .legal li::marker {
    color: var(--accent-deep);
  }

  .legal a {
    color: var(--accent-deep);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .related-pages {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
  }
</style>
